Subject: arm64: dts: exynos7870-on7xelte: configure the Wi-Fi host-wake pin

The BCM43430 host-wake line (gpa2-2) has a pin group upstream,
wlan_hostwake (as an output), that nothing references. Without a pin
configuration the line reads low all the time on the SM-G610F, so the
level-low out-of-band interrupt fires about 18000 times per second:
every time brcmfmac reads an empty intstatus over SDIO, which keeps a
kworker ~40 % busy and adds ~35000 function-call IPIs per second (seen
the same on 6.15 and 7.3.4).

Make the group an external interrupt input with the pull-up and apply it
with the mmc1 pins. Measured on 7.3.4 (cable in, idle, 60 s): host-wake
interrupts a few per second, total interrupts 550/s instead of 70000/s,
context switches 460/s instead of 70000/s, CPU busy 0.6 % instead of
12-16 %.

(Removing the out-of-band interrupt instead, i.e. in-band SDIO
interrupts, also stops the storm; IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH stops the
firmware from coming up.)

Against: linux v7.3.4 + 0001-0013. License: GPL-2.0 (kernel DTS).

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos7870-on7xelte.dts
@@ -865,7 +865,12 @@
 	#size-cells = <0>;
 
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
-	pinctrl-0 = <&sd1_clk &sd1_cmd &sd1_bus1 &sd1_bus4>;
+	/*
+	 * wlan_hostwake: the Wi-Fi host-wake line needs its EINT function and
+	 * the pull-up, otherwise it reads low all the time and the level-low
+	 * out-of-band interrupt below fires ~18000 times per second.
+	 */
+	pinctrl-0 = <&sd1_clk &sd1_cmd &sd1_bus1 &sd1_bus4 &wlan_hostwake>;
 
 	mmc-pwrseq = <&pwrseq_mmc1>;
 
@@ -988,7 +993,7 @@
 
 	wlan_hostwake: wlan-hostwake-pins {
 		samsung,pins = "gpa2-2";
-		samsung,pin-function = <EXYNOS_PIN_FUNC_OUTPUT>;
+		samsung,pin-function = <EXYNOS_PIN_FUNC_EINT>;
 		samsung,pin-pud = <EXYNOS_PIN_PULL_UP>;
 	};
 };
